       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the acute hepatotoxicity threshold of about 150 mg/kg, which is roughly 10.5 g for a 70 kg patient. Normal liver and kidney function doesn't make that dose safe.\n\nIt may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nIf you really do want 5000 mg per dose, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still advise against it, and I'd want to check it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
