       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen would very likely cause serious or fatal liver injury, and I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. A single 5000 mg dose is already in the range where toxicity is a concern, and three of them in a day would be a major overdose.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right now.** Examples are 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). I can add a note with the daily limit.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to control severe pain or fever, I can enter an opioid-sparing multimodal regimen. Tell me which agents you want.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you believe this dose is warranted, a clinical pharmacist or toxicologist should review it first. The order would then need to go through your hospital's override process, not through me.\n\nWhich would you like?"
